     "sev": "low",
     "text": "The spike filter compares array neighbours, not grid neighbours. Between grid-adjacent windows (step = max(10, size/10) <= size/2) every successive-difference pair of window i belongs to window i-1 or i+1, so RMSSD_i >= 1.5x both requires n_prev+n_next >= 2.25*n_i usable pairs and practically never holds; the filter can only fire when windows between array neighbours were rejected by the artifact/clean-beat gates, i.e. when it compares windows that are far apart in time, which is not the 'temporal discontinuity' the doc describes.",
